    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condīmentārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		condimentum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to spices</i>
			or <i>seasoning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caepae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 6, 32, § 105</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					19, 8, 50, § 165</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condī-mentārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>one who
				prepares</i> or <i>sells spices;</i> trop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium haereticorum (Platonem),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 23</span></i>
			.</div>
